@startuml
/' docs/sds/diagrams/plugin-install.puml — package to enabled plugin, in-process (D36).
   Implements: SDS §8, §13.3. Register: C-8 (WITHDRAWN by D36 — no runner, no socket),
   C-9 (no publisher CA, D27), C-13 (migration grammar), O-36 (asset guard), O-37 (test report),
   O-44 (write-only secrets). This diagram deliberately draws no containment boundary,
   because there is none: §13.3.7. '/
title Plugin install, enable, and the in-process hook boundary
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam maxMessageSize 120
skinparam ParticipantPadding 10

actor "Tenant owner" as O
participant "app admin" as APP
participant "app process\n(plugin module)" as PLG
participant "site.db" as DB

== Install: signature, review, DDL ==

O -> APP : upload plugin-<id>-<version>.tar.gz
APP -> APP : verify package root signature\nfirst-party key, or one the OWNER imported
alt unknown signature or revoked root
  APP --> O : 409 SKW_E_PL_SIGNATURE / SKW_E_PL_REVOKED
end
note right of APP
  **No publisher CA** (C-9 / D27). Under D36 the
  fingerprint buys **identity and tamper detection**,
  not containment. The install screen says so.
end note
APP -> APP : validate plugin.json\nid · cms range · main · hooks[] · tables[] · export class
APP -> APP : require test-report.json for this app_image_digest
alt report missing or stale
  APP --> O : 409 SKW_E_PL_TESTS_STALE
end
APP -> DB : BEGIN IMMEDIATE · host-executed migrations\ncreate_table · add_column · create_index · drop_index\n+ asset guard trigger per asset_key column
APP -> DB : cms_plugin_installed(enabled=0, manifest_json, root_hash)\nCOMMIT · postcondition: cms_* | u_* | p_* | sqlite_*

== Enable: import, activate, register ==

O -> APP : enable  (capabilities listed, fingerprints shown)
APP -> APP : re-verify root hash · cms range · realpath under the package root
APP -> PLG : import( …/index.mjs?tenant=<key>&act=<seq+1> )
note right of PLG
  The cache-buster is load-bearing: Node caches
  ES modules by URL, so without `?act=` a
  disable→enable returns the OLD namespace with
  its timers alive. One instance per (tenant,
  plugin, activation) keeps state from crossing
  tenants — an accident-preventer, not a boundary.
end note
PLG --> APP : activate(ctx) — the only window in which ctx.on() is open
APP -> APP : registry.commit(tenant, id) · closeActivation()
APP -> DB : UPDATE cms_plugin_installed SET enabled=1, activation_seq=seq+1
note right of APP
  Any failure above (import, shape, activate,
  register) rolls the registry back, sets
  status='failed' and raises an admin notice.
  The site keeps serving; no hook was registered.
end note

== Runtime: hooks and the facade, one layer ==

O -> APP : a page renders, or posts to a public endpoint
APP -> PLG : dispatch(snapshot(tenant), hook, args)
PLG --> APP : value | throws | never settles | blocks the loop
APP -> APP : a filter may replace ONLY the value it was handed —\nnot status, headers, Set-Cookie or the route
APP -> PLG : store.insert(table, row) · declared columns, row ≤ 32 KiB
PLG --> APP : row described; the HOST writes it on the tenant's admin-write
APP -> DB : assert database_list = ['main'] · ATTACH is unexpressible
APP --> O : 200

note over APP, PLG
  **Facade (14, §8.3):** store.insert/update/delete/query/count · settings.get/has/set ·
  assets.resolve · mail.send · log.write · util.now/random/hash.
  **Not on the facade:** sql · exec · prepare · db · attach · pragma · fs.* · net.* ·
  fetch · env · tenant.* · cms.*. Not on the facade is **not** absent from the process:
  a plugin can `import('node:fs')` or open `data/control.db` itself (§13.3.7).
end note
note over APP, PLG
  **One layer, one witness.** The grant is read from cms_plugin_installed inside this
  request, before the connection is touched. Delete the check and plugin-scope S3 goes
  red — there is no second layer behind it to catch a bypass (§13.3.7).
end note

alt the hook throws, returns the wrong type, or never settles
  APP -> APP : use the value passed in · count the failure · log it
  APP --> O : the page still renders (200), core behaviour for that hook
end
alt three failures in 60 s
  APP -> APP : status='failed' · enabled=0 · registry pruned · admin notice
  APP --> O : 503 SKW_E_PL_UNAVAILABLE on its endpoints; pages unaffected
  note right of APP
    Recovery is an operator action, not a half-open
    retry: `skwctl plugin enable`, or the admin's retry.
  end note
end
alt the hook blocks the event loop synchronously
  note over APP, PLG
    **Nothing happens.** No timeout interrupts a running function in the same thread:
    every tenant's pages stop until the process restarts or the plugin is disabled from
    a shell (`skwctl plugin disable <id> --tenant <key>`). Accepted cost — §13.3.6.
  end note
end

@enduml
